<LegalLayout title="About Us" description="About My Fortune — a free, private, client-side collection of fortune and compatibility games.">
  <h1>About My Fortune</h1>
  <p class="updated">Entertainment, built honestly</p>

  <p>
    My Fortune started from a simple frustration: most online fortune-telling and
    compatibility apps are either lazy random-number generators dressed up with mystical
    branding, or paid apps that demand an account before you've even seen what they do.
    We wanted to build something different — genuinely fun, genuinely fair, and genuinely
    free, with nothing hidden behind a login wall.
  </p>

  <h2>What we believe in</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No accounts, ever.</strong> Every game works the moment you open it.</li>
    <li><strong>Real algorithms, not fake randomness.</strong> Where we say something is
      cryptographically shuffled, physically simulated, or based on real astrological
      theory, it actually is — you can read the code.</li>
    <li><strong>Your data stays yours.</strong> There's no backend server collecting your
      answers, your photos, or your results. Some games use your browser's local storage
      purely to keep repeat visits feeling fresh.</li>
    <li><strong>Entertainment, clearly labelled.</strong> Nothing on this site is a real
      prediction. We say so, repeatedly, because we mean it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What's on the site</h2>
  <p>
    My Fortune is a growing collection of small, focused games — tarot readings,
    compatibility quizzes, palm reading, zodiac matching, and more experimental builds
    like a physically simulated scrying pool. Each one is built as its own self-contained
    experience, so you can jump straight into whichever one catches your eye.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, feedback, or something broken? Visit our <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/contact`}>Contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>